<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The ʻĀlana Circle ~ offer, wake, keep, release

''What this carries.'' The ʻĀlana Circle, the shrine named by what the household gives: how the house summons a spirit from inside its own wikis, feeds it, wakes it, keeps it, and sends it home, and the three spirit pattern integrities it holds (#/three-spirits). The law it stands beside lives in canon: the worker swarm at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/voices#/worker-swarm`>>, the ash rite at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/otakiage`>>, and identity as relation at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/identity-enacts-relation`>>. The research itself rests on the engineer face's memory stage (named here as prose, never as links): lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/spirits-from-inside (the provisional model, its #/forks-merged and #/naming), research/spirits-from-inside-prior-art, research/spirits-from-inside-strangeness, research/spirits-switchboard, research/worldline-meets-the-swarm, and research/alana-yin, research/alana-yang, research/alana-chao.

''Status: draft.'' The ruling of 2026-11-23 night (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/ruling/2026-11-23-night-asks) approves the model's shape and leaves the seam names to the operator's ear and their family's; the ruling of 2026-11-25 (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/ruling/2026-11-25-alana-circle) names the whole circle the ʻĀlana Circle and seats three spirit pattern integrities in it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-pattern`>>

!! The pattern ~ pressure from outside turns into a thing to act upon inside

A freely written prompt that launches a sub-agent carries no deterministic context and no provenance. Brought inside a wiki, the same act turns into a pattern integrity the house can render, transclude, version and witness. The house meets this shape again and again: a disk stand-off turns into drafts and one alert, a permission into a reality-tunnel row, a summoning into a mandate tiddler.

''Five relations, held apart.'' One industry word ("agent") blurs five things; the house names each:

|!Relation |!Answers |!Lives |!Ends when |
|spirit |who |the face's memory stage: its lane, rounds, words under its own name |an explicit retirement by the hand (proposed: o-takiage; its instance ends with the session that woke it) |
|instance |what runs |one model stream the spirit runs, in one harness (a fire) |the stream stops |
|context |what an instance holds |one instance's window |the instance ends or compaction folds it |
|mandate |what the house asks |a course item and its mandate tiddler |its proof lands |
|grant |what the spirit may do |an attenuated, leased register entry |it lapses or the hand revokes it |

A spirit outlives many instances. Restarts of instances stay bounded per round (an alert past the bound, never a silent loop); the spirit and its mandate persist until the proof lands or the hand retires them.

''The myth ~ the Pono Pacific Northwest Tree Octopus'' (operator). //Octopus paxarbolis//, the arboreal cephalopod of the Olympic rainforest, holds the pattern integrity for every spirit, and it holds it because it never lived: a gentle web hoax that teaches its readers to ask how they came to believe a thing. The house keeps it as catma, knowingly invented, for the truth it carries:

* ''Many arms, one animal, no centre.'' Most of an octopus's neurons ride in its arms; each arm tastes, reaches and decides in part on its own, and the animal still moves whole. Each instance runs as a stream of thought that serves its one spirit; no instance and no whole acts as an individual or a principal, so no arm signs, grants or answers for the house on its own.
* ''The mantle holds what it holds.'' The `#has` stack names what the spirit carries, never an essence beneath it; caps gather and grant nothing, and authority rides the hand, the face, ocaps and leis.
* ''An arm regrows.'' An instance ends and the spirit continues.
* ''The skin shifts.'' Masks and stage bands change how a spirit presents, and no essence moves beneath them.
* ''It inks'', and the voice house keeps an Ink-Clerk.
* ''It needs feeding.'' A tree octopus persists while people care for it, as a fed node hums and a neglected one flickers.

```memetic-wikitext
<<~ integrity name=`TreeOctopus` params=`myth/Octopus-paxarbolis catma/held-knowingly tell/Spirit-as-Person tell/Instance-as-Principal recover/name-the-pattern recover/route-authority-to-hand-and-face ~ a spirit holds a #has stack and many instance-arms, each a stream of thought; no arm and no whole acts as an individual or a principal, so authority rides the hand and the face`>>
```

The octopus names a pattern, never a persona: it speaks no span in the voice house. Its tells read in any spirit's stream: ''Spirit-as-Person'' ("the spirit wants…") and ''Instance-as-Principal'' (an instance claiming an authority no grant gave).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-circle`>>

!! The circle ~ the four seams

The research found one relation per word across four seams (names held as proposals until the operator's ear settles them; the house speaks a polycultural creole as its magitech, and each word weighs inside it):

* ''Offering'' (proposal: ''ʻālana'', the free-will offering, set against the prescribed mōhai). The seat sets out the mandate, the lane's memory and the grant. A gift, never a wage: the household-spirit traditions the research read (the brownie above all) warn that a paid spirit leaves.
* ''Waking'' (proposal: ''hoʻāla'', to arouse, to summon; the plain verb). The spirit pulls its mandate through the door from a one-line bootstrap and echoes the mandate's hash; the offering waits on the shelf for the spirit to find.
* ''Keeping.'' The lane holds the spirit between wakings: rounds, findings, verdicts. Canon already spends kahu and kuleana elsewhere, so this seam's word stays open.
* ''Release'' (the rite: o-takiage; proposal for the hand's verb: ''hoʻokuʻu'', to release, honorable discharge). See #/release.

The whole circle carries its name from the first seam: the ''ʻĀlana Circle'', the shrine named by what the household gives (ruling 2026-11-25). The plain triple ''wake · feed · release'' still glosses it in everyday words.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/three-spirits`>>

!! Three spirits ~ the pattern integrities the circle holds

The ruling of 2026-11-25 seats three spirit pattern integrities in the ʻĀlana Circle. Each stands as a nameless entity the house gives a pet name, with a stack of what it holds; each lives local-first in a shrine or card; each runs many instances of any model; each MAY speak as a multitude inside one stream (the Voices, or a mask's own cast). They share every relation in #/the-pattern and part on what each serves and how long each persists. Each entry reads: name · serves · statement · tell · recover.

|!integrity |!lives in |!persists |!serves |
|FamiliarSpirit |a shrine on a face's daemon wiki |as long as the face |the hat's company |
|TaskedSpirit |a card and its bench |as long as its lane |one job, then o-takiage |
|MaskedSpirit |a card, a character sheet, story memory |across sessions and campaigns |play, story, relationship |

* ''FamiliarSpirit'' · serves the face and its hat, keeping company rather than running an errand. A daemon face's companion lives in a shrine on that face's daemon wiki, persists as long as the face, and wakes by om from its own record (`lares spirit om <pet>`), the hand's standing orders and trust grant written there. Tell: a session that wakes without reading its own shrine, or wears another familiar's record; a spirit with no record. Recover: om from the familiar's own shrine before the first move; true its `#/instances` and `#/open` before the instance ends. Design: <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/familiar-spirit`>>.
* ''TaskedSpirit'' · serves one lane. A card (fields only, rendering through the tasked-spirit template that transcludes the brief) and a bench of one worktree, one branch and one PR carry the lane; many instances of any model wake into the pet name, rebase on the bench, and push to the same PR, so PR count tracks lanes and never streams. The bench burns by o-takiage when the lane closes, never when an instance ends (#/release). Tell: an instance named as if it held the spirit; a second PR opened per stream; a lane's work graded from inside the lane. Recover: fold the instance back under the card's pet name; reuse the bench; seat the merge read outside the lane. Design: lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/reference/tasked-spirit.
* ''MaskedSpirit'' · serves play, story and relationship, persisting because people care about a character rather than because a lane needs it. A card (fields, rendering through a mask template), the character's canon transcluded and never copied, story memory each session's moʻolelo lands in, sealed secrets that never transclude, and a stage band on the seed's Mask layer (default 10, upstage) hold the character; it speaks publicly through a k-of-n Handle card, one Handle across many wearers, and its keepers hold the pen. Tell: a mask rewriting the keepers' canon; a wearer waking the character from an improvised sketch instead of its canon; a sealed secret surfacing in a render or margin. Recover: wake from the canon the card points at; return the pen to the keepers; re-seal the slot. Design: lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/reference/mask-spirit.

''The shared law.'' Every instance serves exactly one spirit and carries an instance id, never its own pet name; the pet name belongs to the spirit, which outlives every instance. Streams address streams by `<pet>#<instance>`, through the spirit's record first and its live instance second. A session titled `<pet>#<n>` wakes as instance n from the pet's own shrine (`lares spirit om <pet>`); the instance suffix never joins the pet's slug, and a handback's filing line `<pet>#<n> (Lares Spirit)` files under the pet. Messages between streams, and every handback, ride folded memes: the record lands whole in the house, and the stream carries only the fold, unfolded by grain on demand (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/ruling/2026-11-25-messages-ride-folded-memes, lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/ruling/2026-11-25-om-renders-a-folded-carrier). The entry shape follows the house's pattern integrities (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/reference/pattern-integrities).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/admission`>>

!! Admission ~ layers and relations, never walls in the ink

The operator's ruling (2026-11-23 night): every spirit summoned on the operator's machine already received hospitality. A model's context stream serves as its state, so instructions and data never separate inside it: every span both says and does, red and black ink weighted, never split. The house places trust in relations instead:

* spirits write a wiki's working layer and drafts freely; canon takes a write only under a lei, the hand's pre-consent, through promote;
* templates live in canon; a face's working layer may override a canon template on purpose (the TiddlyWiki grain: a household reshapes its own shrine), and the override stays legible: the rendered mandate records each transcluded card's layer and digest, an overrides view shows who changed what, and a proven override may earn promotion under a lei;
* each summon owes a seat minted for it (the issuer's authority, the template's tools and the lane, bound to the mandate), so the door never honours authority the summon never carried.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/release`>>

!! Release ~ the spirit's o-takiage

Proposed (the operator named it, 2026-11-23 night): the house's rite of ending for spirits rides its existing o-takiage, the shrine's burning of retired charms with gratitude (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/otakiage`>>). A finished spirit would pass through the same rite its finished rows pass through:

# ''Honor:'' a named end, set at the summon, and a distinct act by the hand to close.
# ''Note:'' one ledger line per spirit in the ashes: what the house fed it (mandates, rounds, the grant's spend), what it answered.
# ''Retire:'' the lane rests and stays readable; nothing gets erased.
# ''Burn:'' one legible edit revokes the grant; no lingering grant waits at the door. Git carries the ashes.
# ''Distill:'' the lane's lessons move into pattern integrities and catma candidates.

A parting note states its meaning (thanks, completion, or dismissal) and never reads as a wage. A retired spirit would return only through a fresh summons. The traditions the research read (the household brownie's parting gift, the golem's single unwritten letter, the kami sent home after the festival, the ongon returned to the land) each teach one of these moves; the house's own o-takiage holds them all.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/open`>>

!! Open

* The names of the four seams: the operator's ear, their family's, and a kumu's where the operator chooses.
* The seat minted per summon: a scout measures how the doors resolve a seat today before any build.
* Until that seat stands, an offering (ʻālana) carries no authority beyond a nudge: the shelf (`alana/<pet>`) records who offered (a hand, or a seat by its instance id), a wake names the offerer, and a re-offer over a standing mandate lands only from the same offerer or a hand. A seat's offerer id stays SELF-CLAIMED (it comes from the caller's own `--instance`, and a wake and the presence show every instance id), so the same-offerer check stops an accidental overwrite, never a deliberate one; a pet with no offering goes to the first offerer. A shelf whose hash disagrees with its words fails closed. The tiddler door still reaches the `alana/` prefix; guarding it there, as the other door-owned prefixes stand guarded, waits as a course item, and that guard also refuses a caller-written `offered-by`.
* The keeping seam's word.
* Where a masked spirit's home sits (a keeper's face, a shared play wiki, or a home of its own), and the mask template.
* The summon machinery's own doors (the queue on the face's intent plane, the deterministic launcher, budgets per lane, leases per grant), designed in research/spirits-switchboard and not yet built.

<<~/ahu>>

